# Optional. ICE servers for the live-session video rooms, as a JSON array.
#
# The default is a public STUN server, which is enough for most home networks.
# STUN cannot traverse symmetric NAT, though — corporate networks and some
# mobile carriers — and for those peers a TURN relay is the only thing that
# works. If video connects for some participants and not others, this is the
# first thing to check.
#
# VITE_ICE_SERVERS=[{"urls":"stun:stun.l.google.com:19302"},{"urls":"turn:turn.example.com:3478","username":"user","credential":"pass"}]

# Optional. External error reporting in the browser (PRD NFR-1;
# src/utilities/monitoring.js) — read at BUILD time, so set it before
# `npm run build`. Unset, the Sentry SDK is never downloaded: it is a chunk of
# its own (~160 KB gzipped) that only a build with a DSN asks for.
# Crashes and unhandled errors are sent with no personal data: no user, no
# cookies, and no URL query string or fragment (a reset link carries its token
# there). The same DSN as the server's SENTRY_DSN may be used.
#
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>
